From 82ceadf3e241b5a04c406ee6d5e2fe4c37785172 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Sotraidis <56282582+chrissotraidis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:19:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Aurora: SDL3 UIKit scene geometry in the SDL patch chain

Adds cmake/patches/apply-sdl3-uikit-scene-geometry.cmake to the vendored
Aurora's SDL PATCH_COMMAND, after the Android auto-mapping patch. It is the
SDL 3.4.x UIKit correction shared with the other SDL3 Pad ports
(chrissotraidis/wiicompiled#28, galaxypad-engine#1); its edits are exact and
idempotent and stop the configure if the SDL source does not match. With it,
SDL runs the app only in the application scene it started in, leaves an
external display's scene to the system (mirroring or an extended display),
adopts a replacement scene if iOS discards the first, and takes orientation
from that scene's effectiveGeometry instead of statusBarOrientation (unknown
in scene apps on iOS 27). visionOS keeps upstream behaviour, and non-UIKit
platforms do not compile the edited files.
